	Greetings, hackers!

	It bothers me that lots of questions come up that are
easily answered by a peek in the spoilers, and typically several people
will jump on the bandwagon and answer them.  Whenever something really
out-of-the-ordinary comes up, there is silence across the net.  Does 
anyone know if the dev team is listening?  I've heard people talk about
the most amazing things happening to them (of course I don't remember any
of them, brb) and not heard a single reply; meanwhile whenever someone
wants to know why they can 'see right through' themself or how to get
Excalibur or why they keep dying on level 1, there is no lack of responses
(many of them given by people who haven't looked in the spoilers themselves
or read the source code or, heck, even tried explore-mode).

	Well, now that I have that off my chest, I'll ask ONE MORE TIME:

	Has anyone other than myself run into the situation where a level
in hell had no maze, but rather, regular rooms (specifically a bones level)?

If so, is it a bug or was it done on purpose?

